## 2026-08-21 — Task: Re-add the IRMAA cliff vertical lines to the tax torpedo graph

Third of the ten items the step-by-step rebuild bullet was cut into.

### The lines were never removed

Last iteration's write-up already said so, and `git show 5fe9854 -- src/App.tsx`
confirms it: the four `ReferenceLine`s and their `IRMAA {tier}` labels survived
the tab deletion untouched, along with `cliffsOnChart` and the four
`App.chart.test.tsx` cases that assert on them. So the first half of the bullet
was a no-op and the second half — "the lines need enough label on the torpedo
chart to stand alone" — was the whole task.

### Why the price did not go into the on-chart label

The obvious fix is `IRMAA 1 · +$1,052/yr` on the line itself. It does not fit.
At the default single scenario the three cliffs land at $85,845 / $112,845 /
$146,845 of other income on a $150,000 axis — the third is 98% of the way
across, and at 2026 figures it is $149,876, $124 from the right edge. A
centred label there already reaches past the 28px right margin at
`IRMAA 3` (~50px wide); at ~110px it would be half-clipped by the SVG. The gap
between lines 1 and 2 is ~125px of an ~692px plot area, so the wider labels
would also touch each other. Rotating them along the lines would give room but
puts vertical text over the area curve.

So the label stays the short tier badge, and the price goes in a key directly
under the chart, tied to the lines by a red dashed swatch.

