## Iteration: the front door (21 Aug 2026)

`README.md` opened "# Growth Projector — See peaks and valleys of marginal tax
rates", which is the framing commit d1cf5b3 replaced on the page itself, and
`package.json`'s `name` was still `growth-projector`. Both now say what the app
is: a page called "How Much Can You Take Out This Year?", four steps, one
answer.

### What the README says now

Same order a reader meets the app in. The hook first — one more dollar out of
an IRA drags Social Security in behind it and shoves a gain out of the 0% band,
so the cost is nothing like the bracket. Then the four steps with one sentence
each, then what `tax.ts` prices, then the query-string share format, then the
commands, then a layout table, then deployment, then the not-tax-advice line
the page already carries.

Two things earned their own paragraph because a newcomer cannot infer them:

- **The frozen thresholds.** $25k/$34k and $32k/$44k do not index while
  everything around them does, and that contrast is the reason the year
  selector exists at all rather than a footnote to it.
- **The shelf rule.** Nothing outside `src/shelf/` imports from it, a test
  enforces that, and un-shelving is a `git mv` in the same commit as the
  section that renders the module. That is the one convention in this repo a
  contributor can violate without noticing.

### Three claims checked rather than copied

The backlog's original idea dump — which the old README's subtitle came from —
says LTCG stacking shows "marginal rates over 49%". The page never states that
figure, so I probed the engine directly with a throwaway test rather than
repeat it: `marginalRateCurve` peaks at **40.7%** (single, $40k benefit,
$150k axis) and `ltcgMarginalRateCurve` at **33.7%** (single, $40k other
income, $40k benefit) — 15% flat for the MFJ case I tried. 22.2% and 40.7% are
on the page at App.tsx:2108 and reproduce exactly; 49% does not, so the README
says the compound figure runs "well past the statutory 15%", which is the claim
step 3's explainer actually makes. Temp test deleted.

Two more, both off by one on a first draft:

- The closing recap has **seven** figures, not six — `Room to convert` is the
  seventh and it is the one that answers the h1, so leaving it out of the
  summary was the worst possible omission.
- **Nine** states taxed benefits in 2025, **eight** in 2026: West Virginia's
  exempt share phases 35→65→100% and `stateTax.ts:175` says the count drops.
  A flat "nine" would have been wrong for half the years the page prices.

### The rename

`growth-projector` → `tax-torpedo` in `package.json` and both places in
`package-lock.json`. Nothing imports the package name — `vite.config.ts`'s
`base` is `/congenial-octo-spork/`, which is the repo, not the package — so
this moves no build output.

`npm install` after the rename also pruned 27 `"extraneous": true` lockfile
entries (esbuild 0.28.2 platform binaries left over from some earlier install).
Checked the diff line by line: 27 removals, all extraneous, and the only
additions are the two name lines. Kept rather than hand-reverted, because CI
runs `npm install` and would prune them anyway.

### Verified

`npx tsc -b`, `npx eslint src --max-warnings 0`, `npx vitest run` (9 files, 581
tests, green — unchanged, this iteration touched no source), `npm run build`,
