## The README's front door sends readers to a different application

The bullet was one defect and one decision, and it said so. Fixed the defect,
recorded the decision as its own bullet, and did not make it.

### The defect, confirmed live

Both URLs answer 200 and both are this repo:

```
https://ecao310.github.io/congenial-octo-spork/         <title>Marginal Tax Rate</title>
https://ecao310.github.io/congenial-octo-spork/preview/ <title>How Much Can You Take Out This Year? — Retirement Tax Torpedo</title>
```

`origin/main` is `74a8dea`, package `growth-projector`; `origin/dev` is
`66b19c2`, package `tax-torpedo`. `git rev-list --left-right --count` now says
**0 / 77**, not the 75 the bullet was written against. README.md:12 named the
first one as **Live:**, so the front door sent every reader to the app this one
was rewritten out of. Nothing failed, because nothing failing is the whole
shape of it: two live URLs, two valid pages, and the wrong one is a good page.

### What changed

**README.md** — the link moves to `/preview/` and gains the sentence that
makes it checkable: `` `dev` is the working branch, and that URL is where it
publishes ``, then what the bare URL is instead and why one repo publishes two
apps. The Deployment section already described the mechanism correctly, so it
only gained the consequence it had left unsaid — while `main` is the
pre-rewrite app, the production URL is not this page — and a pointer to the
test below.

Also corrected `npm run test # vitest, 665 tests` to 680. It was stale by 15
and sits in a file this run was already editing.

### The part that is not prose

A link rots the moment the branch under it moves, so `the front door` in
`src/meta.test.ts` derives the right answer instead of restating it:

1. reads the **Live:** URL and the working branch out of README.md's own prose;
2. reads every `.github/workflows/*.yml`, pairing each with the branch it
   fires on and the base it builds with — `--base=` when the job overrides it
   (`deploy-preview.yml`), `vite.config.ts`'s `base` when it does not
   (`deploy.yml`);
3. asserts exactly one workflow deploys the working branch, and that the
   **Live:** path is that workflow's base;
4. asserts the set of `ecao310.github.io` URLs the README names is exactly the
   set the workflows publish — no typo'd path, no URL nothing serves.

It went into `meta.test.ts` rather than a new file because that file's stated
job is already the outward-facing surfaces no other test reads.

**Mutation-checked three ways**, each restored after:

| mutation | result |
| --- | --- |
| **Live:** back at the bare URL | red: `expected '/congenial-octo-spork/' to be '/congenial-octo-spork/preview/'` |
| working-branch sentence says `main`, link left at `/preview/` | red, the same diff inverted |
| a `…/staging/` URL added to the prose | red on the third case |

First draft used vitest's `expect(actual, message)` form. It runs — the
messages printed — but the installed types are single-argument, so `tsc -b`
failed on both call sites. Rewrote to compare *paths* rather than whole URLs:
no message needed, and the diff is short enough that vitest stops eliding the
half that differs, which the full-URL version did (`'https://ecao310.github.io/congenial-o…'`
against itself).

### The decision I did not make

Merging 77 commits to `main` replaces what the production URL serves for
everyone already holding it, and retires `deploy-preview.yml` — whose entire
reason to exist is rebuilding main's site verbatim so that URL never changes
under it. The bullet itself called it "a real decision rather than a chore".
It is now bullet 10 of Backlog 6, marked as needing a human, with the four
things one commit would have to carry. The test is built so that half of them
cannot be forgotten: change the working-branch sentence and the link has to
follow, or the suite goes red.

