interest in total income, but excludes QCD."
================================================================

### The bullet, split first

It arrived as one `[ ]` holding four sub-items. Split into four bullets,
each keeping its own wording verbatim; this run did the first. The other
three — the step-1 summary naming the advanced inputs, the check against IRS
figures, and stripping meta references out of the prose — are now the next
three items in Backlog 7.

### What was actually wrong

`totalIncomeFor` (tax.ts:970) has always been right: `ordinaryIncomeAfterQcd
+ ltcg + ssBenefit + muniInterest`, muni in and the gift out, with a comment
saying why and seven tests on it at tax.test.ts:776. So the arithmetic was
never the defect. The defect was in the three places that hand the reader
that arithmetic to do:

- `CustomTooltip`'s head — "Total income $X · $B SS + $O other income"
- step 2's opening line — "from $X to $Y — the $B benefit set above, which
  does not move, plus $0 to $M of other income"
- the plot's `aria-label`, which is the same sentence for a listener

All three named the benefit and stopped. Measured in a real browser at
$3,750 of tax-exempt interest: the opening line said the axis began at
$28,602 beside arithmetic that reached $24,852. Off by the muni slider,
exactly, in a sentence whose whole purpose is to let the reader add it up.

The figcaption under the axis was already correct — `axisIncludes` /
`axisCaption` (App.tsx:1138) lists both parts and the gift — which is why
this stayed invisible: one of the four sentences about the axis had been
fixed and the other three had not.

### The fix

Two consts beside `axisCaption`, off the same `axisIncludes` list:

- `axisFixedProse` — the part of a figure on this axis the income slider
  cannot move, as prose. Falls back to `$0 of Social Security` when both are
  zero, which is what the aria-label already said in that case, so the
  default reading is unchanged to the character.
- `axisGiftClause` — `, less the first $G of it given straight to charity`.

"The first ... of it" rather than a flat subtraction, and that phrasing is
the one real decision here. `qcdFor` caps the gift by the ordinary income
there is to take it out of, so at the axis's left edge no part of a $26,750
gift has happened yet and that edge is the fixed part on its own. A flat
"less $26,750" reads true at the right edge and is wrong by the whole gift
at the left one — and this sentence names both edges by figure, so it would
have been visibly wrong. Confirmed in the browser: with muni $3,750 and gift
$26,750, `$24,852 + $3,750 = $28,602` at the left and
`$24,852 + $3,750 + $150,000 − $26,750 = $151,852` at the right, both
matching the figures the sentence quotes.

Step 2's opening line lost "which does not move" — "a fixed" carries it in
three fewer words, and the alternative was "neither of which moves" on a
branch.

The tooltip head gained ` + $I tax-exempt` when muni is set.

### What was considered and left

The tooltip head's own addition still does not close when a gift is set:
at $92,500 of other income it quotes $94,352 and breaks out
`$24,852 + $3,750 + $92,500`, which is $121,102. That is by construction —
the x-axis is income *before* the gift, so the head's terms are the axis
figure taken apart — and the lime line directly beneath it exists to say so:
"Less $26,750 given straight to charity — $65,750 of it reaches the return".
The gift has a correction sitting under the head in its own colour, with two
tests on it (App.test.tsx:1506, :1520). Tax-exempt interest had nothing of
the kind, which is what made it the defect and not this. Left alone rather
than adding a fourth term the lime line would then repeat.

`axisCaption` also left alone: it names the contents of a figure, not the
ends of a span, so it offers no addition to fail.

### Tests

660 → 667. One new block, `the axis, taken apart`, which reads the dollar
figures back out of the prose with a regex and adds them up rather than
matching a sentence — so it holds whatever the wording becomes. Seven cases:
the default reading unchanged, muni in both edges, the gift off the front
and not off the left edge, both set at once, the aria-label the same way,
and the tooltip head with and without muni.

Mutation-checked by pasting the old prose back at all four sites: 5 of the 7
go red — the two that pin the unchanged default reading stay green, which is
the point of having them.

