## Make the graph shift right when QCD increases (21 Aug 2026)

Picked up mid-flight. The working tree already held the source half of this
bullet, uncommitted, with 11 tests red — a previous run ended between editing
`totalIncomeFor` and updating the suite. Finishing it was this iteration.

### The change that was already there, and why it is right

`totalIncomeFor` used to subtract the gift. That reads well as a sentence — a
dollar sent straight to charity never reaches the filer — and it drew a chart
that could not be read. 408(d)(8) moves every threshold on this page out by
exactly the gift; an axis that also took the gift off moved every one of them
back by the same amount and landed them where they started. Dragging the
charity slider changed nothing on screen. That is the bug the bullet names.

So the axis carries the gift now: `ordinaryIncome + ltcg + ssBenefit +
muniInterest`, no `ordinaryIncomeAfterQcd`. Line 4a of the return says the
dollar left the IRA; only 4b knows about the exclusion. `agiFor` and `acaMagi`
still subtract it — the tax is unchanged, only the denominator moved.

Confirmed in Chrome against `vite preview`, MFJ/senior/$38,292 SS/$3,750 muni
at $95,000 of other income:

    qcd $0       torpedo starts ~$66K on the axis, tax $10,028, rate 12%
    qcd $60,000  torpedo starts ~$126K on the axis, tax  $1,296, rate 18.5%

Exactly $60,000 of slide, and the flat run the gift buys is $60,000 wide
instead of collapsed onto one x. Total income holds at $137,042 across all
three, so the saving shows up as a smaller numerator rather than hiding inside
a shrinking denominator.

### The caption

    Total income ($), including $38,292 of Social Security and $3,750 of
    municipal interest. Excluding all qualified charitable distributions from
    the tax on it.

The bullet's own text, bar four words. "From the tax on it" is there because
the gift is now *in* the figure the first sentence quotes — a bare "Excluding
all qualified charitable distributions" sitting under an axis that includes
them would be a false statement about the axis, and it would read as a third
item in the "including" list going the other way. What the gift excludes is
the tax, which is what the second sentence now says. No dollar figure, because
`qcdFor` caps the gift by the ordinary income there is to take it from, so any
figure here would be wrong at the left edge.

"Municipal interest" per the bullet, replacing "tax-exempt interest" in this
caption and the chart's aria-label. That leaves the tooltip and the closing
answer still saying "tax-exempt" — logged under Discovered work rather than
swept here.

The step-1 intro and the chart's accessible name both lost their `less the
first $X of it given straight to charity` clause: the span is a plain addition
again, fixed part to fixed part plus every dollar the slider reaches. The
gift's whole effect on that sentence is that `axisMax` grows, which the
